research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-28-{"id":"def-totally-bounded-uniform-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Encyclopedia of Mathematics defines precompactness by finite uniform-cover refinement, equivalently finitely many entourage balls. The item adopts the standard name totally bounded and the entourage formulation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-29-{"id":"lem-ultrafilters-on-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-cauchy","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. This is the standard ultrafilter characterization behind precompactness, and the finite-cover proof is elementary, but the located Encyclopedia source states only the surrounding completion/precompactness theorem rather than this exact all-ultrafilter proposition. It is established, not novel. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The finite entourage-ball cover plus ultrafilter primeness argument is the standard proof that every ultrafilter on a totally bounded uniform space is Cauchy. This familiar lemma is established mathematics extracted from the classical compactness equivalence.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-30-{"id":"lem-compact-uniform-spaces-are-complete","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Complete_uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Compact uniform spaces are standardly complete, and the item gives the usual cluster-point proof, but the located Encyclopedia discussion has already imposed separatedness while this item correctly allows nonseparated uniformities. The broader statement is established but not an exact source match. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Compact uniform spaces are classically complete via the cluster-point argument for Cauchy filters. Separation is needed for uniqueness, not for existence of a limit, so the nonseparated local convention is a standard broadening rather than a novel result.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-31-{"id":"lem-compact-uniform-spaces-are-totally-bounded","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Compact uniform spaces are standardly totally bounded, with the usual finite entourage-ball subcover proof. The located Encyclopedia statement sits under a separated-uniformity convention, while this item is broader, so the hypothesis delta precludes exact-source treatment. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The finite-subcover proof from entourage-ball neighbourhoods is the standard theorem that compact uniform spaces are totally bounded. The argument does not require separatedness, making the local convention delta established and mathematically routine.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-32-{"id":"thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Complete-plus-precompact implies compact is standard, but the item explicitly assumes only the ultrafilter lemma, whereas the source works classically. The local proof verifies that weaker assumption; its extra full-Choice citation is an A3 defect. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Complete plus totally bounded implies compact is a classical uniform-space theorem. The proof through convergence of ultrafilters uses precisely the ultrafilter lemma; making that weak-choice hypothesis explicit is a standard foundational calibration, not invention.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-33-{"id":"cor-uniform-compactness-equivalence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Compact iff complete and totally bounded is standard, but the item records the precise ultrafilter-lemma assumption for the reverse implication. No located source states that same foundational calibration. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The compactness equivalence is the classical combination of compact-implies-complete, compact-implies-totally-bounded, and the converse. Its explicit ultrafilter-lemma scope is a faithful foundational restatement of established mathematics.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
